        body: "If your trip includes meetings or visits in Silicon Valley, **Caltrain** is the rail connection that matters. Express trains from **San Francisco (4th & King)** reach Palo Alto in about an hour, with stops at Millbrae (where you can transfer to BART), Redwood City, and Mountain View. Google, Apple, and Meta campuses are all a short bus or bike ride from Caltrain stations.\n\nThe 4th & King terminus is in the South of Market (SoMa) neighbourhood, walking distance from Oracle Park (the Giants' baseball stadium) and a short Muni ride to Market Street. Caltrain is not integrated with BART fares, so you will need a separate Clipper card balance or ticket — though the Clipper card itself works on both systems. If Silicon Valley access is a daily need, staying in SoMa near the Caltrain station is more practical than Union Square, where you would add a fifteen-minute Muni ride each way.\n\nAt Millbrae station, Caltrain and BART share a platform, creating a useful transfer point. If you are flying into SFO and heading directly to the South Bay, you can take BART one stop to Millbrae and transfer to Caltrain without entering the city at all. For visitors attending conferences at the Moscone Center in SoMa, the 4th & King Caltrain station is a ten-minute walk — closer than most BART stations."
